      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a risk assessment model for a residential property insurance portfolio in the Midwest. We've been seeing a spike in larceny and theft claims in certain ZIP codes over the last 3 years. Looking at the census data alongside our claims data, there's been a pretty significant shift in the ethnic composition of these areas recently. From a statistical modeling perspective, how much weight should I be giving to changes in demographic diversity when trying to predict future theft rates in these specific zones?",
